<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armada del Mar del Sur</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as South Sea Armada</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Armada</a> del Mar del Sur (South Sea Fleet) was the Spanish naval force based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/callao">Callao</a> that guarded the Pacific coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a>. From the late sixteenth century it escorted the annual shipments of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potosi">Potosí</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> from Callao to Panama, where the bullion was carried across the isthmus to the fleets bound for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and it defended the coast against English and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> raiders.</p></div>
